      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-221756",
      ":question/problem": "Let $n$ be an integer. Prove that $a\u2261b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,10)$ if and only if $a\u2261b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,2)$ and $a\u2261b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,5).$\n\n*Hint: You may wish to make use of the following result:* \n\n$$\n2\\cdot (-2)+5\\cdot 1=\\text{gcd}(2,5)=1\n$$"
    }
